5112090008.content:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Account Executive, Public Sector - India&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an India Public Sector Account Executive at Anthropic, you&#39;ll drive the adoption of safe, frontier AI within the Indian government and public sector space, establishing and growing our presence in this strategic market. You&#39;ll leverage your consultative sales expertise and deep understanding of the Indian public sector landscape to propel revenue growth while becoming a trusted partner to customers, helping them embed and deploy AI while uncovering its full range of capabilities. In collaboration with GTM, product, policy, and marketing teams, you&#39;ll help define our market entry strategy and value proposition for the Indian public sector.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is an AI safety and research company that&#39;s working to build reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our customers and for society as a whole. Our interdisciplinary team has experience across ML, physics, policy, business and product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Anthropic&#39;s market entry and expansion in the Indian public sector, establishing our presence and building relationships with key stakeholders across central and state government departments, ministries, and agencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle for Indian public sector opportunities, from initial outreach through to successful deployment, with a focus on building long-term strategic partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate the unique procurement requirements, security standards, and compliance frameworks specific to Indian government technology adoption, including GeM (Government e-Marketplace) and other procurement channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with policy teams to ensure alignment with Indian government AI strategies, the IndiaAI Mission, and Digital India initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage actively with government-led AI initiatives, including participation in forums like the India AI Impact Summit and state-level AI conferences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute innovative sales strategies tailored to the Indian public sector environment, meeting and exceeding revenue targets while maintaining strong relationships with procurement teams and decision-makers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide market intelligence and feedback to product teams to ensure our offerings meet Indian public sector requirements, use cases, and regulatory considerations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain relationships with relevant systems integrators (including TCS, Infosys, Wipro), technology partners, and government digital transformation partners in the Indian market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and document best practices for Indian public sector engagement, creating playbooks that can scale our presence in the market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a leader within the broader public sector team, sharing insights and collaborating on cross-market opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of enterprise sales experience in the Indian public sector, with a proven track record of driving adoption of emerging technologies across central and state government departments&lt;/li&gt;
