&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with EMEA sales teams to create a community-driven pipeline — translating ambassador and event activations into qualified leads and sales opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and track the metrics that matter: event coverage, ambassador retention, community growth, and — critically — the downstream impact on pipeline and conversion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Anthropic in the EMEA developer and builder community, including speaking at conferences, contributing to online developer and builder communities, and building relationships with key technical influencers and builders in the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with marketing, product, and communications teams to ensure community activations are aligned with broader brand and go-to-market strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in developer relations, community management, or a closely related growth or marketing role, with a track record of scaling programs across multiple markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand how to build and run developer or builder communities — from online engagement to in-person events — and can translate that experience into repeatable, scalable programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a track record of identifying unmet needs in a market and building new programs or initiatives from scratch to address them — not just executing existing playbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong experience working in or across EMEA markets and understand the nuances of localizing a global strategy for different regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience working across time zones with a US-based or globally distributed team, and are comfortable with the communication rhythms and async workflows that requires&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable working at the intersection of community and commerce — you understand how community programs can generate business impact, and you can build the attribution frameworks to show it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have enough technical depth to engage credibly with developers and builders (e.g., familiarity with APIs, LLMs, or software development workflows), even if you don&#39;t write production code day-to-day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are a strong communicator who can write clearly, speak at conferences, and build trust with both internal stakeholders and external communities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in ambiguous, fast-moving environments and are comfortable being an early hire in a region with significant room to shape the approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Speak English fluently and are proficient in at least one other European language (German or French preferred; open to Italian or Spanish)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong candidates may also:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience with developer advocacy, technical content creation, or conference speaking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a background in go-to-market strategy or market expansion at a high-growth technology company&lt;/li&gt;
