5138232008.content:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Head of Travel &amp;amp; Expense, you will be the single owner of everything T&amp;amp;E at Anthropic: employee, guest and executive travel policy, private charter strategy, our Navan and Brex platforms, preferred hotel and airfare programs, duty-of-care (in partnership with Security), and Board-level reporting on executive expenses. You will report to the Head of Finance Operations and lead an initial team of two, with a mandate to build a best-in-class program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a rare opportunity to come in as a true builder—inheriting solid operational foundations and a Claude-first culture pioneering AI-powered automation across Finance—and architect a T&amp;amp;E program worthy of a company shaping the future of AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy, Policy &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and own Anthropic&#39;s multi-year T&amp;amp;E strategy, evolving the function from operationally sound to best-in-class across policy, cost management, employee experience, and compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a comprehensive global T&amp;amp;E policy framework—employee, executive, and international—embedding controls directly in systems to drive compliance at the point of booking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a cross-functional T&amp;amp;E governance structure with Finance, Security, Legal, HR, and Executive Assistants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and enforce jurisdiction-specific T&amp;amp;E policy frameworks for international entities (EMEA, APAC), incorporating local per diem regulations, VAT reclaim eligibility, and country-level receipt/documentation requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor Negotiations &amp;amp; Savings&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the corporate travel supplier program, driving material savings through hotel RFPs, airline corporate agreements, and preferred rate programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage strategic relationships with our T&amp;amp;E travel and expense systems, serving as the primary business contact for contract negotiations, product roadmap discussions, and AI feature development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report savings performance to Finance leadership and executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Travel &amp;amp; Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the subject matter expert for all executive travel needs, vendor selection, and utilization governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal and Finance on executive travel tax implications, business purpose documentation, and audit-ready recordkeeping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform &amp;amp; AI Automation (Claudification)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and optimize Anthropic&#39;s T&amp;amp;E-related systems and platforms: configuration, policy rules, approval workflows, virtual cards, and ERP integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion AI-powered automation across T&amp;amp;E—deploying Claude to audit transactions, flag policy exceptions, and automate reporting—consistent with Anthropic&#39;s Claude-first culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of T&amp;amp;E / corporate travel experience at a high-growth technology company, including 7+ years in a leadership or program ownership role with direct reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of cost savings: material, quantified outcomes from hotel RFPs, airline corporate agreements, and travel supplier negotiations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep platform expertise in Navan and/or comparable TMC platforms, plus Brex or equivalent expense management tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive travel program ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional instincts: proven ability to partner across Security, Legal, HR, Finance, and C-suite executive teams and their supporting staff&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Duty-of-care and international compliance: background in travel risk management frameworks and T&amp;amp;E compliance across global entities (EMEA, APAC, LATAM)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-curious builder mindset: experience deploying AI tools to automate T&amp;amp;E processes, or genuine enthusiasm for doing so—and comfort creating structure where none exists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$300,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$360,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education requirements: &lt;/strong&gt;We require at least a Bachelor&#39;s degree in a related field or equivalent experience.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
